steps:
Styles: in theme.css update tokens to navy #0B1F3A, white, accent #1F8A8A (plus existing shades and a darker premium navy and pale teal-grey surface). Add --text-display at 2.5rem on phones and 3.75rem (60px) on desktop, an 8px-based spacing scale and soft card shadows. In global.css:
- serif headings and sans body;
- hover lift on cards;
- fade/slide-in done in CSS only: content is never hidden in the prerendered markup and needs no JS to become visible; any IntersectionObserver is guarded with `typeof IntersectionObserver !== 'undefined'` inside useEffect;
- `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` removing animations, transitions and transforms;
- navy gradient overlays behind text on photos;
- img { max-width: 100%; height: auto }.
Use system fonts only, with no @import of remote CSS, no external URLs, no CDNs, scripts or analytics. Every class used in markup has a CSS rule.

